\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Full-data bounded power law MLE fits are skewed down from the true power law coefficient due to the tail decay. Select lattice sizes $L = 5, 30, 100$ are depicted. The fits for all lattice sizes are depicted in Appendix Figure \ref {fig:APPENDIX_powerlaw_mle_viz}. MLEs are drawn as black points with a connecting line drawn for illustration purposes. The left column shows avalanche size, the centre column shows avalanche area, while the right column shows avalanche $L_1$ length. The dashed vertical lines represent the fixed parameter $x_{max}$.}}{11}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:powerlaw_fitted_mle}{{3.3}{11}{Full-data bounded power law MLE fits are skewed down from the true power law coefficient due to the tail decay. Select lattice sizes $L = 5, 30, 100$ are depicted. The fits for all lattice sizes are depicted in Appendix Figure \ref {fig:APPENDIX_powerlaw_mle_viz}. MLEs are drawn as black points with a connecting line drawn for illustration purposes. The left column shows avalanche size, the centre column shows avalanche area, while the right column shows avalanche $L_1$ length. The dashed vertical lines represent the fixed parameter $x_{max}$}{figure.caption.7}{}}
